  "_knownGaps": {
    "_": "Things published recipes ask for that this kitchen genuinely does not have, listed so the matcher reports them as MISSING with a real name rather than as UNKNOWN. Everything here has been hit by an actual rejected recipe.",
    "hondashi": "Japanese dashi powder, dried bonito and kelp. Rejected Aaron and Claire Ground Beef Gyudon on 2026-08-11. Chicken bouillon covers the salt but not the oceanic depth.",
    "kimchi": "Suggested alongside two Korean dishes, never required by one.",
    "gochujang": "Korean fermented chilli paste. Rejects most spicy Korean recipes.",
    "gochugaru": "Korean chilli flakes. Not the same as crushed red pepper: coarser, fruitier, much less hot.",
    "pancetta": "Rejected three separate frittata recipes on 2026-08-12. Bacon is the usual stand-in.",
    "tinned tomatoes": "Rejected the metric bolognese on 2026-08-11. NOTE: fresh grape tomatoes arrived 08-12, which changes what is possible but is still not the same product.",
    "kidney beans": "Blocks chilli con carne.",
    "enoki mushrooms": "Stringy, stays in strands. Cremini is meatier and not equivalent, though it works.",
    "wine": "No red or white wine in the kitchen. Blocks a lot of braises and many ragu recipes.",
    "heavy cream": "No cream. Milk is not a substitute in anything that reduces.",
    "sesame seeds": "Toasted sesame seeds, wanted as a garnish by most Korean recipes.",
    "pickled ginger": "Benishoga, garnish on gyudon. Marked optional by its own recipe.",
    "short grain rice": "Not owned. Long grain works but changes the dish: in a donburi the sauce is meant to soak a sticky layer of rice under the topping, and long grain stays separate so the sauce runs to the bottom of the bowl. About $5.77 and it unlocks every donburi plus the Beef Bulgogi pot rice already written.",
    "potatoes": "No regular potatoes. The sweet potato is not a substitute in anything roasted or mashed: different sugar, different texture, and it collapses.",
    "fresh coriander": "Also sold as cilantro. None in the kitchen. Parsley looks similar and tastes nothing like it, so it is not a swap.",
    "fresh chilli": "No fresh chillies of any colour, scotch bonnet and thai chilli included. The crushed red pepper and crushed jalapeno bring heat but not the fresh fruity flavour.",
    "fish sauce": "No fish sauce. Soy sauce is saltier and not funky, so it changes a Thai or Vietnamese dish substantially.",
    "fresh mint": "No mint.",
    "coconut milk": "No coconut milk. Nothing here substitutes for it in a curry.",
    "pork": "No pork of any cut, including chops, belly, shoulder and mince.",
    "chorizo": "No chorizo. Also covers most cured sausage.",
    "shallots": "No shallots. Onion is the usual stand-in, but shallots are milder and sweeter.",
    "cabbage": "No cabbage, white or red. The frozen salad mix is not the same thing cooked.",
    "leek": "No leeks.",
    "mustard": "No prepared mustard or mustard powder. The honey Dijon vinaigrette is a dressing, not a substitute.",
    "bread": "No bread, baguette, pita or breadcrumbs. There IS flour and yeast, so bread is a project rather than an ingredient.",
    "prawns": "No prawns, shrimp, squid or salmon. Tilapia is the only fish and it is frozen.",
    "lamb": "No lamb.",
    "worcestershire sauce": "No Worcestershire sauce.",
    "feta": "No feta. Parmesan, mozzarella and Monterey Jack are the three cheeses here and none behaves like feta.",
    "warm spices": "No cinnamon, nutmeg, allspice, cardamom, cloves, turmeric, saffron, garam masala or curry powder. The rack has paprika, smoked paprika, cumin, garlic powder, onion powder, Italian seasoning, Cajun and chilli flakes, and that is all of it.",
    "bean sprouts": "No bean sprouts.",
    "peanuts": "No whole or crushed nuts of any kind. There is peanut butter, which is not a garnish.",
    "ham": "No ham or bacon.",
    "lemongrass": "No lemongrass.",
    "tinned fish": "No tinned tuna, salmon, sardines or anchovies. The only fish here is frozen tilapia.",
    "brown sugar": "No brown sugar, only white.",
    "self raising flour": "No self-raising flour, but plain flour and baking powder are both here.",
    "fresh soft herbs": "No thyme, sage, rosemary, tarragon, oregano, bay or chives, fresh OR dried, and no mixed-herb blend. The only herbs here are fresh parsley, fresh dill, fresh basil and the Italian seasoning blend. This row and the staples list used to disagree, and the staple was winning.",
    "green vegetables": "No broccoli, asparagus, green beans, cauliflower, pak choi, spring greens, kale or spinach. The vegetables here are onion, carrot, peppers, sweet potato and whatever is in the frozen mixed bag.",
    "avocado": "No avocado.",
    "curry paste": "No Thai red, green or yellow curry paste, and no Indian curry paste. Not something the spice rack can approximate.",
    "asian pantry": "No hoisin, tamarind, fish sauce, chipotle paste, miso, gochujang or curry leaves. Soy, oyster sauce, mirin, Shaoxing and sesame oil are the ones that ARE here.",
    "sour cream": "No soured cream, creme fraiche, buttermilk or yogurt substitute for cooking. There is Greek yogurt, which splits if boiled, so it is not a swap in a hot sauce.",
    "vanilla": "No vanilla extract, paste or pods.",
    "beans": "No tinned beans of any kind: kidney, pinto, cannellini, black, chickpeas or butter beans.",
    "tinned sweetcorn": "No tinned sweetcorn or green chiles. There IS frozen corn.",
    "salsa": "No salsa, barbecue sauce or taco sauce.",
    "spirits": "No brandy, rum, whisky or liqueur.",
    "root veg": "No parsnip, swede, turnip, celeriac, fennel, radish or beetroot.",
    "steak": "No steak cuts. The beef here is 4.5 kg of raw mince in the freezer plus one bag of browned mince. Mince is not a swap for a steak in anything where the cut is the point, and the sliced sirloin from the August roast is finished.",
    "other spices": "Not on the rack: chilli powder, cayenne, five spice, white pepper, mustard powder, all-purpose or taco or steak seasoning. The rack is paprika, smoked paprika, cumin, garlic powder, garlic salt, onion powder, Italian seasoning, Cajun, crushed red pepper and crushed jalapeno, and that is all.",
    "whole chicken": "No whole chicken or bone-in chicken pieces beyond the thighs and wings in the freezer. The frozen ground chicken is mince and is not a roast.",
    "poultry mince": "No ground turkey. The only poultry mince here is frozen ground chicken.",
    "condiments and jams": "No chutney, jam, marmalade, molasses, hoisin-style sweet sauces or barbecue sauce. Ketchup, mayonnaise, pesto, sriracha, relish and the two vinaigrettes ARE here.",
    "other rice and grains": "No risotto, arborio, paella, sushi, short-grain, brown or wild rice, and no quinoa, couscous, bulgur or cornmeal. Long grain white and Minute instant ARE here, and they behave differently: long grain will not go creamy for a risotto."
  },
